    <!-- ⚠️ config_autoBrightness{Brightening,Darkening}LightDebounce were set here
         to 2000/3000 and are GONE, because on this path they are dead resources.
         The live values now live in
         configs/displayconfig/display_port_147.xml, installed to
         /vendor/etc/displayconfig/.

         They read back correctly — `cmd overlay lookup android
         android:integer/config_autoBrightnessBrighteningLightDebounce` on the
         device returned 2000, which is exactly why this looked done — and yet
         `dumpsys display` reported the debounce as -1. The reason is that the
         only caller of loadAutoBrightnessBrighteningLightDebounce() is
         loadAutoBrightnessConfigValues() (DisplayDeviceConfig.java:2467-2472),
         which runs from initFromFile() alone. Without a DisplayDeviceConfig XML
         the device takes initFromGlobalXml() (:1947-1959), which calls
         loadAutoBrightnessConfigsFromConfigXml() — that builds the brightness
         mapping and nothing else. The resource fallback inside the loader is for
         a DDC file that omits the tag; it is not a config.xml path.

         Keeping them here as well would be two places that must agree for no
         benefit, since this copy can never win and can never be reached.
         This is the same shape as the tree's other "written but not reachable"
         findings — see the config_defaultNightMode note in
         configs/partition_order.xml. -->


