    <!-- Attaching the folio keyboard put every app into a freeform desktop
         window. That is not this tree's choice and it is not AOSP's default
         either: core/res/res/values/config.xml:7559,7562 ship both of these as
         false.

         ONE of them is turned on underneath us by an inherited STATIC overlay,
         which is why it does not appear anywhere in this device tree:

             vendor/lineage/overlay/common/.../config.xml:90
                 config_isDesktopModeSupported        -> true   (every device)

         ⚠️ The second line here used to say that
         "vendor/custom/overlay/tablet/.../config.xml, line 19" sets
         config_canInternalDisplayHostDesktops true for every tablet — and that
         is a PixelOS path which does not exist on LineageOS.
         (Written without the colon-number form on purpose: it is a dead
         citation, and work/scripts/34-citation-check.py would otherwise try to
         resolve it forever.)
         vendor/lineage/overlay/tablet/ contains only two files, both about the
         glanceable hub, and neither touches this resource — so
         config_canInternalDisplayHostDesktops is already false from AOSP and the
         override below is REDUNDANT. It is kept anyway, for the reason stated
         further down: the intent is "this tablet does not host desktops", and
         stating it once leaves the next reader wondering whether the other half
         was missed. Redundant and explicit beats absent and inferred.

         Static overlays are baked into framework-res.apk, so an RRO always wins
         over them — no partition-order question here, unlike config_defaultNightMode.
         Verified on the device before writing this: `cmd overlay lookup` in
         verbose mode reported both resolving from framework-res.apk itself with
         no competing RRO in the chain, while config_showNavigationBar on the
         same run showed "Overlaid: /vendor/overlay/FrameworkOverlayMalbec.apk".
         (Spelling the flag out is not an option here: a double hyphen is illegal
         inside an XML comment and aapt2 only reports it about 73% into a build.)

         The gate is DesktopStateImpl.kt:53-59:

             isDeviceEligibleForDesktopModeDevOption =
                 if (!enforceDeviceRestrictions) true
                 else (isDesktopModeSupported && canInternalDisplayHostDesktops)
                      || isDesktopModeDevOptionSupported

         enforceDeviceRestrictions comes from
         persist.wm.debug.desktop_mode_enforce_device_restrictions, unset here, so
         it defaults true and the two resources below are live. The third term,
         config_isDesktopModeDevOptionSupported, is false in AOSP and nothing in
         this tree or its inherited overlays sets it — checked, not assumed.

         Both are written even though the expression is an AND and one would do:
         the intent is "this tablet does not host desktops", and stating it once
         leaves the next reader wondering whether the other half was missed.

         ⚠️ Known cost, accepted by the owner: desktop windows on an external
         display go away too. This is a Wi-Fi-only tablet with no wired display
         output in use. -->
    <bool name="config_isDesktopModeSupported">false</bool>
    <bool name="config_canInternalDisplayHostDesktops">false</bool>

